  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A$ and $B$ be two square matrices of order 3 such that $|A|=3$ and $|B|=2$. Then $\\left|\\mathrm{A}^{\\mathrm{T}} \\mathrm{A}(\\operatorname{adj}(2 \\mathrm{~A}))^{-1}(\\operatorname{adj}(4 \\mathrm{~B}))(\\operatorname{adj}(\\mathrm{AB}))^{-1} \\mathrm{AA}^{\\mathrm{T}}\\right|$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
